          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "21. Find the molecular mass of nitric acid (HNO ). Atomic mass — H = 1 u; "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "N = 14   u ; \\; O = 16   u ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.689,
            0.517,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "22. Find the molecular mass of methane (CH ). Atomic mass "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "C = 12   u ;  H = 1   u ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.75,
            0.662,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9.8 Formula Unit Mass of Ionic Compounds"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.774,
            0.775,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In ionic compounds, the collection of the simplest whole number ratio of ions is termed as a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "formula unit",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". The mass of a formula unit is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "formula unit mass",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 31,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.832,
            0.242,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 9.6"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 32,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.853,
            0.49,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Formula unit mass of sodium oxide "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( \\mathrm { N a } _ { 2 } \\mathrm { O } )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 33,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.874,
            0.419,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Atomic mass — Na = 23 u; O = 16 u"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 34,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.894,
            0.621,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Formula unit mass of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{Na}_{2}\\mathrm{O}=(23\\mathrm{~u}\\times2)+(16\\mathrm{~u}\\times1)=62\\mathrm{~u}"
            }
          ]
        }
